%S A401746 32,1,2,1,3,2,1,4,0,2,1,0,9,7,2,1,6,14,16,9,32,1,7,20,30,80,11,2,1,8,
%T A401746 27,80,55,36,13,2,1,9,40,77,105,91,49,0,2,1,10,44,112,182,196,0,64,17,
%U A401746 2,1,11,54,156,294,243,336,204,81,19,32,1,12,65,210,405,672,714,540,285,320,21,2
%N A401746 Triangle read by rows: for n>0 and 0<=k<=n, T(n,k) is the number of circular (n+k)-bit strings with k 1's that, when circularly shifted by 5 bits, do not have any coincident 1's when placed over the original bit string.
%C A401746 T(n,k) is the number of tilings of a circular (n+k)-board using k curved (1,4)-fences and n-k curved unit square tiles. A (1,g)-fence is composed of two unit square tiles separated by a gap of width g.
%C A401746 This is the m=5 member in the sequence of triangles A029635, A401743, A401744, A401745, A401746, A402564 which give the number of tilings of a circular (n+k) X 1 board using k curved (1,m-1)-fences and n-k curved unit square tiles.
%C A401746 This is also the m=5, t=2 member of a two-parameter family of triangles such that T(n,k) is the number of tilings of an (n+(t-1)*k) X 1 circular board using k curved (1,m-1;t)-combs and n-k curved unit square tiles. A (1,g;t)-comb is composed of a line of t unit square tiles separated from each other by gaps of width g.
%C A401746 T(n,k) is the coefficient of x^k in (L((n+k)/p))^p where p=gcd(n+k,5) and L(n,x) is a form of Lucas polynomial defined by L(n,x)=L(n-1,x)+x*L(n-2,x) where L(0,x)=2, L(1,x)=1, and L(n,x)=0 for n<0.
%C A401746 For n+k>5, T(n,k) is the number of k-subsets of n+k objects arranged in a circle such that no two objects in a subset are separated by 4 objects.
%C A401746 Sum of n-th antidiagonal (counting initial 32 as the 0th) is (L(n/p))^p where p=gcd(n,5) and L(i) is the i-th Lucas number A000032.
%F A401746 T(n,0) = 1 for n>0.
%F A401746 T(n,1) = n+1 for n>=5.
%F A401746 T(5*k,5*k) = 32 for k>=0.
%F A401746 T(5*k+j,5*k+j) = 2 for k>=0, j=1,..,4.
%F A401746 T(k+1,k) = 2*k+1 for k>=0 if 2*k+1 is not a multiple of 5 and 0 otherwise.
%F A401746 T(k+2,k) = (k+1)^2 if k+1 is not a multiple of 5.
%F A401746 T(k+2,k) = (16/5)*(k+1)^2 if k+1 is a multiple of 5.
%F A401746 T(5*k-1,5*k-4) = 0 for k>0.
%F A401746 T(5*(k+1),5*k) = (2k+1)^5 for k>=0.
%F A401746 T(n,k) = C(n,k)*(n+k)/n if n+k is not a multiple of 5.
%F A401746 T(n,k) = T(n-1,k) + T(n-1,k-1) for n>=4k+2 and k>=0.
%e A401746 Triangle begins:
%e A401746  32;
%e A401746   1,   2;
%e A401746   1,   3,   2;
%e A401746   1,   4,   0,   2;
